# Working artifacts, not source.
# The design brief zip and the concept logo are superseded by
# `design_handoff_dananeh/` and `assets/brand/`; the screenshots are output
# from `scripts/screenshot.js`. They stay on disk, out of the repository.
Expo app design brief.zip
Concept-Logo.jpeg
scripts/screenshot-*.png

# Downloaded release artifacts. An APK is verified by checksum against the EAS
# build record; the binary itself never belongs in the repository.
/artifacts/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks

# Native Firebase configuration.
#
# This app talks to Firebase through the **JS SDK**, which reads its
# configuration from `EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_*` — so `google-services.json` is not
# used by anything here. It arrives with the native migration (React Native
# Firebase, FCM, Crashlytics), and it is per-project: a staging file committed
# once is a file somebody later builds production against.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Per-environment configuration. `.env.example` is the committed one; every
# other `.env*` names a real project and stays on the machine that owns it.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Application Default Credentials, wherever they land.
application_default_credentials.json
*-service-account*.json
